! Source !! First-pass signal
|-
| [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Wikipedias List of Wikipedias] || As of August 2026, 364 editions have been created: 348 active and 16 closed. Editions differ in scale, language, policy, automation, community and navigation.
|-
| [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/List_of_Wikipedias Meta-Wiki List of Wikipedias] || Provides operational statistics and alternate comparison lenses including article count, edits/article, depth, language family, country, speakers/article, quality, creation date and sample coverage.
|}

'''Research method:''' do not manually read 348 editions in sequence. Build a comparative sample first, then expand based on variance.

Suggested first sample archetypes:

* English Wikipedia — scale and policy complexity;
* Simple English Wikipedia — accessibility / simplified language;
* German Wikipedia — stricter editorial culture and review patterns;
* French Wikipedia — large independent community practices;
* Spanish Wikipedia — major global-language edition;
* Japanese Wikipedia — non-Western large edition;
* Chinese Wikipedia — multilingual/script and censorship environment;
* Arabic Wikipedia — regional/language governance and contributor-risk context;
* Cebuano Wikipedia — automation/bot-scale case;
* one small healthy edition;
* one closed edition;
* one Incubator project.

The sample should be selected and documented before conclusions are generalized.

