== Research backlog ==

=== A. Navigation architecture ===
* Compare category/portal/outlines behavior across selected Wikipedia editions.
* Compare how specialist wikis handle subdomains and deep technical navigation.
* Identify when portals outperform a well-designed category + overview + outline combination.
* Test semantic/query-driven portal generation in BITwiki.

=== B. Coverage architecture ===
* Convert the 1,000/10,000 cross-language core lists into a coverage-gap dataset.
* Compare against Wikipedia Vital levels without inheriting English-Wikipedia recentism/bias.
* Compare against BITwiki's existing V1 corpus and current V2 domains.
* Derive candidate Domain additions from repeated coverage gaps.

=== C. Self-administration ===
* Study dashboards, maintenance queues, requested articles, drafts, deletion/discussion systems, portal administration, category discussion, and governance surfaces.
* Design the smallest BITwiki equivalents appropriate to a human+agent knowledge system.

=== D. Comparative wiki dataset ===
* Define a machine-readable schema for wiki/encyclopedia comparisons.
* Populate the first archetype sample.
* Expand only when a new system adds a meaningful architectural pattern.

=== E. Governance and security ===
* Classify controversy patterns: vandalism, capture, brigading, state pressure, legal risk, privacy, conflict-of-interest, misinformation, governance abuse, automation failures.
* Separate content risk from contributor risk and infrastructure risk.
* Feed mature findings into governance only after review.

== Research discipline ==

* Distinguish policy/guideline from essay, proposal, historical page, article, or external criticism.
* Prefer primary project documentation and academic literature for architectural claims.
* Treat Wikipedia as evidence, not as specification.
* Track failures as carefully as successful patterns.
* Do not equate scale with quality.
* Do not assume English Wikipedia conventions generalize to all language editions.
* Do not turn every discovered distinction into a BITwiki namespace, Domain, Entity type, or Property.

